# Phase 1 tables

Use only these five tables until a later phase adds more:

| Table | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `profiles` | One row per auth user (created by sign-up trigger) |
| `series` | Published series catalog (Home rails) |
| `episodes` | Episodes per series (seeded; player comes later) |
| `my_list` | Per-user saved series |
| `watch_history` | Per-user resume state (schema now; UI later if unused) |

No payment, purchase, unlock, or subscription tables in Phase 1.

# Migration requirements

- Explicit `ALTER TABLE ... ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` on all five tables.
- Sign-up trigger function: `SECURITY DEFINER` + `SET search_path = ''`.
- Explicit `GRANT`s so `anon` / `authenticated` can use what RLS allows (do not rely on default privileges alone).
- RLS: users read/write only their own `profiles`, `my_list`, and `watch_history` rows. `series` and `episodes` are publicly readable when published.

# Seed vs CI

- Seed data lives only in `supabase/seed.sql` (e.g. 6 series × 10 episodes).
- Local: `supabase db push --include-seed`.
- **CI never seeds.** CI runs `supabase link` then `supabase db push` without `--include-seed`.

# Environments

- Local and staging work use the staging project only (`tunetalez-staging`).
- Never point a non-production branch at production Supabase.
